{
  "id": "dehumidification___removing_moisture_from_air",
  "title": "Dehumidification - Removing Moisture from Air",
  "description": "Calculator for air dehumidification methods including cooling (vapor condensation), adsorption (silica gel and activated alumina), and absorption of water vapor.",
  "type": "calculator",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Dehumidification Methods\n\nAir can be dehumidified through three main methods:\n\n1. **Cooling** - Condensation of vapor by cooling air below dew point\n2. **Adsorption** - Using materials like silica gel or activated alumina to hold moisture on their surface\n3. **Absorption** - Using absorbent materials like calcium chloride solution\n\nSelect the method below to calculate dehumidification parameters."
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "method",
          "label": "Dehumidification Method",
          "type": "select",
          "options": [
            {
              "label": "Cooling (Vapor Condensation)",
              "value": "cooling"
            },
            {
              "label": "Adsorption - Silica Gel",
              "value": "silica_gel"
            },
            {
              "label": "Adsorption - Activated Alumina",
              "value": "activated_alumina"
            },
            {
              "label": "Absorption",
              "value": "absorption"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "air_mass",
          "label": "Air Mass",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 100,
          "unit": "kg"
        },
        {
          "id": "initial_humidity",
          "label": "Initial Absolute Humidity",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 15,
          "unit": "g/kg"
        },
        {
          "id": "final_humidity",
          "label": "Final Absolute Humidity",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 8,
          "unit": "g/kg"
        },
        {
          "id": "adsorbent_mass",
          "label": "Adsorbent Material Mass",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 50,
          "unit": "kg"
        },
        {
          "id": "reactivation_temp",
          "label": "Reactivation Temperature",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 165,
          "unit": "°C"
        },
        {
          "id": "specific_heat",
          "label": "Specific Heat of Adsorbent",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 1.13,
          "unit": "kJ/kgK"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "moisture_removed",
          "label": "Moisture Removed from Air",
          "formula": "inputs.air_mass * (inputs.initial_humidity - inputs.final_humidity) / 1000",
          "unit": "kg",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "moisture_reduction_percent",
          "label": "Moisture Reduction",
          "formula": "(inputs.initial_humidity - inputs.final_humidity) / inputs.initial_humidity * 100",
          "unit": "%",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "adsorbent_capacity_utilization",
          "label": "Adsorbent Capacity Utilized (Silica Gel)",
          "formula": "inputs.moisture_removed / (inputs.adsorbent_mass * 0.40) * 100",
          "unit": "%",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "reactivation_heat_required",
          "label": "Heat Required for Reactivation",
          "formula": "inputs.moisture_removed * 4800",
          "unit": "kJ",
          "format": "decimal"
        },
        {
          "id": "adsorbent_temp_rise",
          "label": "Temperature Rise of Adsorbent (for reactivation energy)",
          "formula": "inputs.reactivation_heat_required / (inputs.adsorbent_mass * inputs.specific_heat)",
          "unit": "K",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Adsorbent Material Properties\n\n### Silica Gel (SiO₂)\n- **Adsorption Capacity**: 40% of its own mass\n- **Bulk Density**: 480 - 720 kg/m³\n- **Void Volume**: 50 - 70% by volume\n- **Specific Heat**: 1.13 kJ/kgK\n- **Reactivation Temp**: 160 - 170°C\n- **Reactivation Heat**: 4800 kJ/kg water removed\n\n### Activated Alumina (Al₂O₃)\n- **Adsorption Capacity**: 60% of its own mass\n- **Bulk Density**: 800 - 870 kg/m³\n- **Void Volume**: 50 - 70% by volume\n- **Specific Heat**: 1.0 kJ/kgK\n- **Reactivation Temp**: 160 - 170°C\n- **Reactivation Heat**: 4800 kJ/kg water removed"
    }
  ]
}